      "text": " Illa Illa"
    },
    {
      "start": 190.8,
      "end": 198.56,
      "text": " Veed Every day"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.56,
      "end": 206.2,
      "text": " Trishur Joli"
    },
    {
      "start": 206.2,
      "end": 214.22,
      "text": " Gnan Poru"
    },
    {
      "start": 214.22,
      "end": 236.98,
      "text": " doctor doctor um um e e keshavan keshavan kochi kochi teacher teacher"
    },
    {
      "start": 236.98,
      "end": 245.82,
      "text": " with locatives. Form locative phrases by adding il to the words provided. This exercise is similar"
    },
    {
      "start": 245.82,
      "end": 252.46,
      "text": " to section A of the reading practice, but does not parallel it directly. Listen to the model."
    },
    {
      "start": 254.06,
      "end": 262.38,
      "text": " Speaker. Trishur. Student. Trishuril. After the space for you to give your locative phrase,"
    },
    {
      "start": 262.38,
      "end": 267.3,
      "text": " the correct form of the phrase will be given for you to compare and to repeat once again."
    },
    {
      "start": 268.6,
      "end": 273.08,
      "text": " The first group of words end in a consonant, hence add il directly."
    },
    {
      "start": 273.86,
      "end": 278.04,
      "text": " Ready? Listen, form locative phrases, then repeat."
    },
    {
      "start": 292.38,
      "end": 299.38,
      "text": " school schoolil"
    },
    {
      "start": 299.38,
      "end": 303.38,
      "text": " Badras Badrasil"
    },
    {
      "start": 303.38,
      "end": 308.38,
      "text": " Nyungal Nyungalil"
    },
    {
      "start": 308.38,
      "end": 313.38,
      "text": " Texas Texasil"
    },
    {
      "start": 313.38,
      "end": 318.38,
      "text": " Austin Austinil"
    },
    {
      "start": 318.38,
      "end": 324.48,
      "text": " The next group of words ends in half U which drops before IL with one"
    },
    {
      "start": 324.48,
      "end": 341.38,
      "text": " exception which is VIR. VITIL. Similarly, NAT country. NATIL."
    },
    {
      "start": 341.38,
      "end": 348.12,
      "text": " Now listen and form the locative by dropping half u."
    },
    {
      "start": 348.12,
      "end": 350.8,
      "text": " Adh"
    },
    {
      "start": 350.8,
      "end": 355.74,
      "text": " Idh"
    },
    {
      "start": 355.74,
      "end": 360.98,
      "text": " Afis"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.98,
      "end": 365.44,
      "text": " Buk"
    },
    {
      "start": 365.44,
      "end": 375.96,
      "text": " The following words end in a vowel or semi-vowel, hence ad-ya before il."
    },
    {
      "start": 378.12,
      "end": 382.52,
      "text": " Kochi Kochiyal"
    },
    {
      "start": 382.52,
      "end": 388.28,
      "text": " Joli Joliyal"
    },
    {
      "start": 388.28,
      "end": 394.36,
      "text": " Kai Kaiyal"
    },
    {
      "start": 394.36,
      "end": 400.36,
      "text": " Kasera Kaserayal"
    },
    {
      "start": 400.36,
      "end": 404.36,
      "text": " Mesha Meshayal"
    },
    {
      "start": 404.36,
      "end": 408.18,
      "text": " Pena, penayil."
    },
    {
      "start": 411.52,
      "end": 415.7,
      "text": " The last group of words end in am,"
    },
    {
      "start": 415.7,
      "end": 419.56,
      "text": " which changes to double t before il."
    },
    {
      "start": 422.06,
      "end": 425.54,
      "text": " Keralam, keralatil."
    },
    {
      "start": 429.56,
      "end": 433.34,
      "text": " Ernakulam, ernakulatil."
    },
    {
      "start": 434.36,
      "end": 436.36,
      "text": " Pustakam."
    },
    {
      "start": 436.36,
      "end": 439.36,
      "text": " Pustakatil."
    }
  ]
